From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PYXL <72852241+pyxl-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:20:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Luigi's Mansion 3: declare depth_mode zero

The game sets nvnDeviceSetDepthMode near = 0. Without the key the
offline pipeline archive was made for near = -w, the host refused it at
every start and rebuilt 3,852 pipeline pairs before the first frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#580
Reason: Luigi's Mansion 3 sets depth mode near = 0: the profile key lets the bundled pipeline archive match
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#123
---
 dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/README.md | 2 ++
 dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/game.tsv  | 3 +++
 dm/games/README.md                  | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/README.md b/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/README.md
index 361d3baf..87328bcb 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/README.md
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ No `patches.py`.
 
 A deferred renderer: the scene draws into a G-buffer of two integer targets (R32Uint, RGBA8Uint) and a D32S8 depth, light volumes and a full-screen resolve light it into RG11B10F targets, and a chain of 960×540 to 60×33 bloom passes ends in the window. Most textures are ASTC.
 
+- **Resolved: the bundled pipeline archive was refused at every start** (`pipeline archive bundled with the app: made for … depth near=-w …, this run needs … depth near=0`), and the device rebuilt its 3,852 pairs before the first frame (16 s). The game sets `nvnDeviceSetDepthMode` near = 0. **Current:** the profile declares `depth_mode zero`, so the archive holds the `main0_z` vertex entries.
+
 - **Resolved: every scene draw skipped** (`failed to create render pipeline … output of type float4 is not compatible with a MTLPixelFormatR32Uint color attachment`, about 1,400 pixel shaders). With no PC version the translator types every fragment output float, and the G-buffer shaders write bit-packed integers through `as_type<float>`. A hand-written row per shader (`shader_facts_manual.tsv`, Breath of the Wild's way) does not scale to that. **Current:** 1,396 pixel shaders get a second entry point, `main0_u`, that writes the G-buffer as integers (`fs_uint`); the host takes it for a pipeline whose written colour attachments are all unsigned integer formats (`pso_all_uint`).
 - **Current: shadow cascades from an array of driver-table handles** (586 pixel shaders: `array<texture2d_array<float>, 32> fp_t2das_cb2_0`, `shaders with a binding whose slot was not decoded 588`), indexed by (0x80 + a cascade offset) ÷ 8 over the driver table c2 (`c2_array`).
 - **Resolved: the boot aborted in Metal's pipeline validation** (`MTLPixelFormatDepth16Unorm is not color renderable`): a 1024×1024 D16 texture (a shadow) is drawn through an R16 view. Such a pass now draws into a colour shadow of the same pixel size, copied in before and back after the pass (`shrt_block`; D16 and D32F; not D24S8).
diff --git a/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/game.tsv b/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/game.tsv
index 2003f565..8b95071b 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/game.tsv
+++ b/dm/games/0100DCA0064A6000/game.tsv
@@ -50,3 +50,6 @@ pad_layout	full
 # ---- Shader split ----
 shader_groups	/init.dict=init
 shader_note	Luigi's Mansion 3 shaders
+# the NVN depth mode the game sets (nvnDeviceSetDepthMode near = 0, '[nvn] depth mode near=0' in the log): the pipeline archive made offline holds the main0_z vertex entries
+# (dm/gfx/tools/pso_offline.py). Without it the Mac prebuild made near = -w bases, the host refused the bundled archive and rebuilt 3,852 pairs at every start
+depth_mode	zero
diff --git a/dm/games/README.md b/dm/games/README.md
index d5bedb71..7c3c8618 100644
--- a/dm/games/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/README.md
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ One row per profile; the notes are each profile's `README.md`.
 | `alloc_big_align` | `on` / `off` (the default): `nn::mem::StandardAllocator::Allocate` aligns blocks of 64 KB or more to 64 KB (`hle_os.c`). Vanillaware's engine (13 Sentinels: Aegis Rim, Unicorn Overlord) takes a memory pool's storage from malloc and cuts ring heaps out of it at 64 KB alignment relative to the pool's GPU address. On the Switch that address is big-page aligned; the host's is the CPU address, only 4 KB aligned, so the last ring heap does not fit and keeps base 0, and the game writes through a null pointer (13 Sentinels entering its first battle, Unicorn Overlord past the title screen) |
 | `shared_font` | Optional, decided by the game files without it (the SDK version the host reads from the `sdk` module, `loader.c` `dm_sdk_major`, and `main`'s imports, `dm_main_imports`): what the shared-font address points at. `bfttf` (SDK 11 and later, when `main` imports `ScalableFontEngineHelper::Decode`) = the 8-byte BFTTF header (with the "already decoded" marker) followed by the TTF, which Mario passes to `Decode`; `ttf` = the TTF itself, which SDK 10 and older games hand straight to `ScalableFontEngine::LoadFont` (Super Mario 3D World + Bowser's Fury: with the header the engine fails with error 403 and the game crashes looking up a glyph; Odyssey, Link's Awakening, Age of Calamity and Three Houses alike) and Unity's player to FreeType (Patrick's Parabox: with the header its Japanese, Korean and Chinese text drew nothing). No profile sets it |
 | `device_api` | Optional, decided by the SDK version without it: the NVN API version `major.minor` that `nvnDeviceGetInteger` reports, 55.15 for SDK 11 and later (what Mario requires) and 53.313 for SDK 10 and older (`hle_nvn.c` `nvn_api`). Games check it and skip creating their device on a mismatch: Super Mario 3D World + Bowser's Fury (SDK 10) requires major 53 and minor ≥ 313. No profile sets it. `DM_NVN_API` overrides. Not part of the shader chain version (only `shader_*` keys are) |
-| `depth_mode` | `gl` (the default, NVN's near = −w) or `zero` (near = 0): the depth mode the game sets with `nvnDeviceSetDepthMode`, for the pipeline bases made before the game runs: the [pipeline archive made offline](../../docs/development.md#the-pipeline-archive-made-offline) for the iPhone (`main0` or `main0_z` vertex entries; built for a game with `pso_mtl4 on` or with `DM_PSO_GPUS`) and the NSP script's Mac prebuild (`DM_PSO_PREBUILD_DEPTH`). The host itself follows the mode the game sets; a wrong value only costs the device its own prebuild. Great Ace Attorney Chronicles, 13 Sentinels (both releases), Big Brain Academy, Link's Awakening, Engage and ASTRAL CHAIN set `zero` |
+| `depth_mode` | `gl` (the default, NVN's near = −w) or `zero` (near = 0): the depth mode the game sets with `nvnDeviceSetDepthMode`, for the pipeline bases made before the game runs: the [pipeline archive made offline](../../docs/development.md#the-pipeline-archive-made-offline) for the iPhone (`main0` or `main0_z` vertex entries; built for a game with `pso_mtl4 on` or with `DM_PSO_GPUS`) and the NSP script's Mac prebuild (`DM_PSO_PREBUILD_DEPTH`). The host itself follows the mode the game sets; a wrong value only costs the device its own prebuild. Great Ace Attorney Chronicles, 13 Sentinels (both releases), Big Brain Academy, Link's Awakening, Engage, ASTRAL CHAIN and Luigi's Mansion 3 set `zero` |
 | `render_base` | The 3D views' base size, docked then handheld (`1600x900 1280x720`): what `DM_RENDER_SCALE` scales. `settings.py` writes it into the render scale's row of `launcher.json` as `base`, so a front end can show the setting in pixels. Only for a game with a render scale stub, and only a size its note documents |
 | `op_mode` | The operation mode the game sees at start: `console` (the default, docked) or `handheld`. Super Mario Galaxy and Captain Toad: Treasure Tracker use `handheld`: docked, their pointer is the Joy-Con gyro, which the host does not have; handheld, it is the touch screen, which the iPhone front end feeds with the touches no gamepad control takes (in the 3D layout, outside the right third of the screen, which is the right stick; `DmGamepad.m`). Handheld also renders at 720p. `DM_OPMODE=0` / `1` overrides, also from `Documents/env.txt` |
 | `perf_mode` | `follow` (the default): the performance mode follows the operation mode (Boost docked, Normal handheld); `boost`: Boost whatever the operation mode (`hle_oe.c`), a combination a Switch 1 never reports, so a profile choice. Rhythm Heaven Groove plays handheld with Boost: docked means a TV to the game, which then asks for a latency calibration, and only Boost gives its 1920x1080 draw size (handheld Normal draws 1280x720) |
